<DATA=Code>
  2009-01-01 12:00  => IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* SSG-4 (MT-043): one SCAN for every call. Record length, the
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* input name in the end line and the IF R < n limit come from the
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* SGSPARM file written by the skeleton hand-off; see
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* _scratch\spike-scan\spec.md. Print lines as the skeleton.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PROGRAM-ID. 'ASSURFED-UTILIT-SCAN-GN'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => CONFIGURATION SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => SOURCE-COMPUTER.  UNIVAC-1100-60EIS.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => OBJECT-COMPUTER.  UNIVAC-1100-60EIS.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => SPECIAL-NAMES.  PRINTER IS LISTE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FILE-CONTROL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT  PARMF  ASSIGN  TO  DISC SGSPARM.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT  TAPEIN  ASSIGN  TO  DISC SCANIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT  PRT  ASSIGN  TO  PRINTER.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => DATA DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FILE SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FD  PARMF
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     LABEL RECORD STANDARD.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  P-TYPE         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  P-REST         PIC X(78).
  2009-01-01 12:00  => 01  PARM-LEN-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC XX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  PL-LEN         PIC 9(5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     03  FILLER         PIC X(73).
