  2009-01-01 12:00  => OPEN-FILES SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-READ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO M-NAME.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN INPUT PARMF.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-LECT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     READ PARMF AT END GO TO PARM-FIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'IN'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PL-LEN TO P-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'MN'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PN-TEXT TO M-NAME.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-TYPE = 'MX'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE PX-MAX TO P-MAX.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO PARM-LECT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PARM-FIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE PARMF.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     COMPUTE N-CHUNK = (P-LEN + 99) / 100.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FIRST-READ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     OPEN INPUT  TAPEIN.  OPEN OUTPUT  PRT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => LR. MOVE SPACES TO RECIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     READ  TAPEIN  INTO  RECIN  AT END  GO TO END-OUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO REC-AREA.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE WS-IN-LEN TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > P-LEN
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE P-LEN TO CP-LEN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF CP-LEN > 0
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        MOVE RECIN (1:CP-LEN) TO REC-AREA (1:CP-LEN).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO REC-IN-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => TEST-FIELDS.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-MAX > 0 AND REC-IN-CT NOT < P-MAX GO TO LR.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FOUND-REC.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD  1  TO  REC-FOUND-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE ZERO  TO  LINE-CNT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO FIVE-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF FIVE-CT > 9 MOVE REC-IN-CT TO F-CT
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>       WRITE PRT-LINE FROM F-LINE AFTER 1 MOVE 1 TO FIVE-CT
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>      ELSE   MOVE REC-IN-CT TO CT-CT
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>       WRITE PRT-LINE FROM CT-LINE AFTER 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO LINE-CNT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE  1  TO  SKIP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO K.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PRINT-CHUNK.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF K > N-CHUNK GO TO PRINT-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     COMPUTE KP = (K - 1) * 100 + 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE REC-AREA (KP:100) TO WS-CHUNK.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE  PRT-LINE  FROM  WS-CHUNK  AFTER ADVANCING SKIP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO LINE-CNT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO SKIP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO K.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO PRINT-CHUNK.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PRINT-END.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES  TO REC-AREA.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE  1  TO  SKIP.     GO  TO  LR.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => END-OUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE  REC-IN-CT  TO  M-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE REC-FOUND-CT  TO  FN-CT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE PRT-LINE  FROM  M-LINE AFTER ADVANCING 10 LINES.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     CLOSE  TAPEIN  PRT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     STOP RUN.
</DATA>
<DATA=Documentation>
  -MAP-
  Documentation
  * SSG-4 (MT-043): one SCAN for every call. Record length, the
  * input name in the end line and the IF R < n limit come from the
  * SGSPARM file written by the skeleton hand-off; see
  * _scratch\spike-scan\spec.md. Print lines as the skeleton.
  PROGRAM-ID. .
  -MAPEND-
  -MAP-
  Technical issues
  -MAPEND-
</DATA>
<IN FOLDER>
COBOL
</IN FOLDER>
</OBJECT>
